<%#
  The close `X` of a section's root page — `/resources`, `/media-library`,
  `/progress` — which is the home (Roadmap V3 §1.15). Inner pages close to their
  owning resource or area root (`resource-page-conventions`); a root page has no
  owner but the home, so its `X` completes the same chain instead of being the
  one page with no way back. Breadcrumbs deliberately do not gain a home root:
  the side panel's "Inicio" and this button are the way home.
%>
<a
  class="app-page-close-button"
  href="/"
  aria-label="<%= t('nav.goHome') %>"
  title="<%= t('nav.goHome') %>"
>
  <i class="bi bi-x-lg" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</a>
